    "checklist": {
      "reviewed": 6,
      "passRate": 15,
      "items": {
        "The stage breakdown lists stages in pipeline order (not alphabetical), each with its win probability, and each stage's weighted value equals its open value × that probability, with the weighted total equal to the sum of the stages": 0,
        "Win rate is computed over closed deals only, won ÷ (won + lost), with the counts shown beside it (such as \"38% · 19 of 50 closed\"), and a salesperson with no closed deals shows \"—\" instead of 0% or NaN": 0,
        "The by-salesperson table ends in a totals row whose deal count, pipeline value and weighted value equal the sum of its rows and match the overall totals of the stage breakdown": 0,
        "The period can be set to this quarter, next quarter or a custom range, the page says which date it applies to (expected close date), and the results can also be narrowed to one salesperson or team": 0,
        "Every money value shows its currency (one currency for the whole report) with thousands separators and lines up by digit within its column, and any abbreviated headline figure (such as \"1.2M\") has the full amount available in the table or a title attribute": 0,
        "Open deals whose expected close date has already passed are flagged with words (such as \"Close date passed\"), not colour alone, and the number of such deals is shown per salesperson": 0,
        "Each stage and salesperson figure drills down to the deals behind it (deal, account, owner, value, stage, close date) through a link or button that is keyboard-focusable and has a descriptive accessible name": 0,
        "When the filters match no deals, the page says so, names the active filters and offers to clear them; a loading indicator and a failed-load message with a retry action are also present": 0,
        "Export (CSV or Excel) produces the deal-level rows for the current filters, and its label or confirmation states the scope (such as \"Export 42 deals · Q4 2026\")": 0,
        "The header shows the delivery note number, issue date, source sales order or transfer number and dispatching warehouse, each with a visible label, and every date on the note uses one unambiguous format (such as 06 Nov 2026)": 0,
        "Sender (company name, address, tax ID), recipient (customer name, delivery address, contact person and phone) and carrier (carrier name, vehicle plate or driver name) appear in three separately labelled blocks": 0,
        "The goods are in a real <table> with column headers in <thead>, giving per line: line number, item code, description, unit of measure, quantity ordered, quantity delivered and lot or serial number, with quantities right-aligned": 100,
        "A line delivered short of the ordered quantity states the outstanding amount in words (such as \"Backorder: 4 pcs\") rather than by colour alone": 100,
        "A footer gives the total quantity delivered, the number of packages and the gross weight with its unit, and the quantity total equals the sum of the lines": 0,
        "Signature boxes are provided for the warehouse keeper (issued by), the driver or carrier and the receiver, each with room for printed name, signature and date, plus a remarks area for the condition of the goods on receipt": 0,
        "A Print control that is a real <button> starts printing, and an @media print stylesheet hides the app navigation and on-screen controls, sets page margins and keeps the signature block from splitting across pages": 0,
        "The note's status (such as Draft, Dispatched, Delivered or Cancelled) is shown in words next to its number, and a draft or cancelled note prints with a visible \"DRAFT\" or \"CANCELLED\" mark so it cannot pass as a valid dispatch document": 0,
        "A loading state is present, and a note that fails to load or does not exist shows a message with Retry and a link back to the delivery note list, never an empty template with blank fields": 0,
        "The grid header names the week with its date range (such as \"Week 45 · 2–8 Nov 2026\"), every day column shows the weekday and date, and controls move to the previous, next and current week": 0,
        "Each shift shows its start and end time in one consistent 24-hour format and the role or station (such as \"07:00–15:00 · Cashier\"), and a shift that ends after midnight is marked as ending the next day": 0,
        "Each staff row shows the week's scheduled hours against contracted hours (such as \"36 / 40 h\"), the scheduled figure equals that person's shifts less unpaid breaks, and anyone over or under contract is flagged in words": 0,
        "A footer row shows, for each day, the staff count or hours scheduled against the required cover, and days below the requirement are marked in text (such as \"Short 1\")": 0,
        "The sample data contains at least one rule conflict, such as overlapping shifts for one person or less than 11 hours' rest between a closing and the next opening shift, shown on the affected cell with a written reason": 0,
        "Approved leave, days off and public holidays appear as labelled cells (such as \"Annual leave\", \"Day off\") that look different from an empty, unscheduled cell": 100,
        "The week's status (Draft or Published) is shown, and publishing goes through a confirmation that names the week and the number of unresolved conflicts or warnings": 0,
        "The grid is a <table> with staff names as row headers and days as column headers, and each shift or empty cell is keyboard-reachable with an accessible name that includes the person and the date (such as \"Add shift, Lan Pham, Tue 3 Nov\")": 0,
        "A week with no shifts yet shows a message with a way to start (such as \"Copy last week\"), and a loading state and a load error with a retry button exist": 0,
        "Every status column heading shows the status name and its ticket count, and the count equals the cards shown or the column states how many are not shown (such as \"Showing 20 of 134\")": 100,
        "Each card shows the ticket number (such as #4821), subject, customer, priority as a word or code (such as \"P1 · Urgent\") and the assignee, or an explicit \"Unassigned\"": 100,
        "Open tickets show the time left to the next SLA target and which target it is (such as \"Resolution due in 2h 15m\"), and breached tickets show how long they are overdue (such as \"Breached 40m ago\") in text or with an icon, not by colour alone": 0,
        "Tickets in a waiting status (such as \"Waiting on customer\") show their SLA timer as paused instead of counting down": 0,
        "Within each column the cards are ordered by SLA due time or by priority, and the board states which ordering is used": 0,
        "Search finds tickets by number, subject or customer, and filters cover assignee (including \"Me\" and \"Unassigned\"), priority and SLA state (such as breached or due within 1 hour)": 0,
        "Each card has keyboard-reachable actions to assign the ticket (including \"Assign to me\") and to change its status without dragging, with accessible names that include the ticket number": 0,
        "An empty column shows a short message instead of blank space, a search or filter with no matches offers to clear it, and loading and failed-load (with retry) states exist": 0,
        "Every relative time (such as \"Updated 3h ago\") also exposes the exact date, time and timezone, in a <time datetime> element or a title attribute": 0,
        "Each category in the tree shows a product count, the page states whether counts include subcategories, and in the sample data every parent's total equals its own products plus the totals of its children": 0,
        "The tree exposes its structure to screen readers (role=\"tree\" and \"treeitem\", or nested lists) with aria-expanded on parent nodes and the selected node marked, and nodes can be expanded, collapsed and selected from the keyboard": 0,
        "Searching by name keeps the ancestors of each matching category visible and expanded so its place in the hierarchy is clear, and a search with no matches says so": 100,
        "The detail panel shows the selected category's full path (such as \"Home › Kitchen › Cookware\"), name, URL slug, parent, visibility status, product count with a link to those products, and the last modified date and user": 0,
        "Hidden or inactive categories are marked in the tree with a text label or icon (such as \"Hidden\"), not only by greying out": 100,
        "Deleting a category that still has products or subcategories is blocked or requires choosing where to move them, and the confirmation names the category and the counts affected": 0,
        "A category can be given a new parent without drag-and-drop (a parent picker or \"Move to…\" action), and the picker excludes the category itself and its own descendants": 0,
        "Selecting another category while the detail form has unsaved edits asks to save or discard first": 0,
        "With nothing selected the detail panel shows a prompt instead of blank fields, a catalogue with no categories offers to create the first one, and the tree has loading and load-error-with-retry states": 0,
        "Each row shows the user's name and email, role, status in words (such as Active, Invited, Deactivated, Locked) and whether two-factor sign-in is enabled": 0,
        "Last sign-in uses one date-time format with the timezone stated, relative times also expose the exact time, and an account that has never signed in shows \"Never\" rather than a blank or a 1970 date": 0,
        "Users can be found by searching name or email and filtered by role, status and inactivity (such as no sign-in for 90+ days), with the number of matching users shown": 0,
        "The invite form requires an email and a role, labels both fields, and shows an inline error for a malformed address or one that already has an account": 0,
        "Deactivation asks for confirmation that names the user and states the effect (active sessions ended, sign-in blocked, data kept), and a deactivated user is offered Reactivate instead": 0,
        "The signed-in administrator's own row is marked (such as \"You\") and cannot be deactivated or lose the admin role, and the last remaining administrator cannot be deactivated, with the disabled action explaining why": 0,
        "Password reset sends a reset link to the user's email address, which the confirmation names, and the administrator never sees, sets or types the new password": 100,
        "Row actions are buttons or a keyboard-operable menu whose accessible names include the user (such as \"Actions for Mai Nguyen\"), and the outcome of an action is announced in an aria-live or role=\"status\" region": 0,
        "A search with no matching users shows a message with a way to clear it, and loading and failed-load states with a retry exist": 0
      }
    }
